{#- Shared FAQ/disclosure pattern, adapted from the MIT pattern lab's
    "04 / NATIVE DISCLOSURES" study
    (~/.claude/skills/creative-website-design/assets/pattern-lab/index.html).
    Only the idea is reused (native <details>/<summary>, no JS, one item
    open by convention): the markup, classes and copy here are this
    project's own, scoped to css/styles.css design tokens rather than the
    pattern lab's standalone stylesheet.

    Every answer passed in must restate something already said elsewhere on
    the same page or on an already-approved page (business.json, the page's
    own body copy), this macro does not get to introduce a new claim,
    price, promise or credential. Callers own that; this file only renders
    whatever strings they pass. -#}
{% macro faq(items, heading = "Common Questions", eyebrow = "Before You Reach Out") %}
<section class="section faq" aria-label="{{ heading }}">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-head center" data-reveal>
      <span class="eyebrow">{{ eyebrow }}</span>
      <h2 data-reveal-words>{{ heading }}</h2>
      <hr class="rule">
    </div>
    <div class="faq-list" data-reveal>
      {%- for item in items %}
      <details class="faq-item"{% if loop.first %} open{% endif %}>
        <summary>{{ item.q }}</summary>
        <div class="faq-item__body"><p>{{ item.a | safe }}</p></div>
      </details>
      {%- endfor %}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
{% endmacro %}
